# Json.Serializable serialize_property Method Signature

The `serialize_property` method in Vala classes implementing `Json.Serializable` can return `null` and should be declared with the nullable return type.

## Correct Signature

```vala
public Json.Node? serialize_property (string property_name, Value value, ParamSpec pspec)
```

## Examples in Codebase

- [NodePropBase.vala](mdc:src/JsRender/NodePropBase.vala) - Returns `null` for extended class properties
- [JsonSerialize.vala](mdc:src/Palete/JsonSerialize.vala) - Always returns `null`

## Common Pattern

```vala
public Json.Node? serialize_property (string property_name, Value value, ParamSpec pspec) {
    switch (property_name) {
        case "property1":
        case "property2":
            return default_serialize_property (property_name, value, pspec);
        default:
            // Skip properties that don't belong to this class
            return null;
    }
}
```

## Important Notes

- The method can return `null` to skip serialization of certain properties
- This is commonly used in base classes to only serialize their own properties
- Extended classes should handle their own properties and return `null` for others
- Always use `Json.Node?` (nullable) as the return type, not `Json.Node`